  "version": 1,
  "title": "A subexponential upper bound for log c in the abc conjecture",
  "abstract": "For every positive real epsilon, there is a positive constant C such that log c is at most C times rad(abc) to the power epsilon whenever a and b are positive coprime integers and a + b = c. The radical is the product of the distinct prime factors. This is an upper bound for log c. The abc conjecture itself remains open.",
